<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chintamanrao Patwardhan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1774">1774</a>–<a href="/years/1851">1851</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Chintamanrao Appa Saheb</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chintamanrao <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patwardhan">Patwardhan</a>, known as Appa Saheb, was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> chief of the Patwardhan family and the founder of Sangli State. In a division of the family estates in 1782 he separated from the family seat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miraj">Miraj</a> and made Sangli his own capital, later building its fort and Ganapati temple. Sangli became a princely state under British protection, ruled by his descendants until 1948.</p></div>
